   "about": "While classically trained in the art of the electron rather than the byte, Lars has been writing software and self-teaching in some capacity since he was in high school. He would enroll himself in computer science class in college because they were the \"fun\" classes. This gravitation toward software culminated with the release of the iPhone in 2007, at which point it was only natural to shift focus to the mobile platform. By 2011, Lars was writing software for what was then called the \"iPhone OS\" full-time.\n\nHe now enjoys focusing on language-agnostic technical solutions and automated tooling to make humans more efficient authors of software. Deep down he still enjoys a finely crafted artisanal animation or performance tuning a scroll view for buttery-smooth scrolling.\n\nIn his spare time, you will usually find him working on his mountain bike, writing open-source software, or honing design skills in Sketch or Figma.",
